1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,870
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,170
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:05,710
(Episode 9)

4
00:00:06,180 --> 00:00:07,850
Cat got your tongue?

5
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:10,580
Are you sleeping
with your eyes open right now?

6
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:19,660
Pardon? Did you ask something?

7
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:23,860
I guess I must be exhausted.
I'm sorry, Mother.

8
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,060
I didn't hear you properly.

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,970
Dae Chi isn't the type to just sit around
doing nothing like that.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,170
He is not the kind of person
to waste his time so carelessly.

11
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:37,980
He must be exhausted too, Mother.

12
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:41,980
He might have gotten tired
of making meals for himself at home.

13
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:47,450
Listen to you, his own mother.

14
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:51,320
No matter how I think about it,
it feels off.

15
00:00:52,290 --> 00:00:55,160
Take a close look at him
and pull him aside...

16
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:56,530
to ask him what is going on.

17
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,500
Yes.

18
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,210
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

19
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,580
This Kang family.

20
00:01:15,810 --> 00:01:16,820
They are my sworn enemies.

21
00:01:17,950 --> 00:01:20,290
I must have committed high treason
in my past life.

22
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:23,050
How many times
must I have betrayed my country...

23
00:01:23,390 --> 00:01:24,660
to be suffering like this at my age?

24
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:29,330
Mother.

25
00:01:29,730 --> 00:01:33,430
How are you still so sharp
at your age?

26
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,150
He's still sleeping?

27
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:55,050
Hey, Kang Dae Chi.
Wake up, little brother.

28
00:01:55,690 --> 00:01:57,090
It's time to eat.

29
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,760
I'm not hungry.

30
00:01:59,090 --> 00:02:01,890
Hey, I know
I'm an incompetent older brother,

31
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:04,360
but when your elder speaks to you,

32
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,630
you should at least pretend
to get up and listen.

33
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,200
Are you not going to get up?

34
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:12,570
Hey, are you ignoring me too?

35
00:02:17,110 --> 00:02:18,480
Who is ignoring you?

36
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,750
Fine, I'm up. What is it?

37
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:23,820
You know...

38
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:27,550
how I went completely bankrupt,

39
00:02:27,950 --> 00:02:29,650
got divorced
from your sister-in-law,

40
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:32,020
and had no choice but to move
back in with Mom.

41
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:35,990
You know all about
my sad story, right?

42
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:39,230
You didn't get a divorce.
You were dumped.

43
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,530
Let us get the facts straight.

44
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,470
Hey.

45
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:48,640
Legally speaking,
it was a mutual divorce.

46
00:02:51,610 --> 00:02:52,610
Go on.

47
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:55,150
I have never said
this to you before...

48
00:02:55,510 --> 00:02:58,750
because my pride as your older
brother would not allow it,

49
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:02,750
but I'm going to swallow my pride
just this once and ask you. Okay?

50
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:07,460
Little brother, could you...

51
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:10,400
lend me some money?

52
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:19,570
You will, right?

53
00:03:20,570 --> 00:03:22,170
Come on. It's my first time asking.

54
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,740
- Gang Nam.
- Yes, go on.

55
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:27,880
Just speak comfortably.

56
00:03:29,210 --> 00:03:30,250
Listen.

57
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:34,520
My personal rule is that
I never lend money...

58
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:37,090
to siblings, or even family.

59
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:38,560
That is my firm belief.

60
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:40,530
So?

61
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:43,800
You really can't lend it to me...
Wait, no.

62
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:47,330
You won't lend it to me?

63
00:03:48,230 --> 00:03:49,900
Yes, I'm sorry.

64
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:52,340
Please try to understand.

65
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:57,810
- Since you are my brother.
- No, I don't understand at all.

66
00:03:57,940 --> 00:03:59,510
And honestly, right now,

67
00:03:59,910 --> 00:04:01,810
I'm incredibly disappointed.

68
00:04:01,810 --> 00:04:04,520
You graduated from a top university,

69
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:06,850
you work for the best company
in the country,

70
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:09,250
and you keep getting promoted.

71
00:04:09,590 --> 00:04:12,660
I know that you make a huge salary
right now.

72
00:04:13,660 --> 00:04:17,360
But your one and only brother...

73
00:04:17,430 --> 00:04:20,570
never asked you for a handout
whenever my business was struggling,

74
00:04:20,570 --> 00:04:21,900
not even 1,000 dollars.

75
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,300
Why?

76
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:27,570
Because, as you said,
I'm your older brother.

77
00:04:28,170 --> 00:04:30,410
But you are so capable,

78
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:32,840
and I'm asking for help
just this one time,

79
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,610
and you won't help me?

80
00:04:36,850 --> 00:04:38,920
Family? Beliefs?

81
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:41,490
Give me a break.

82
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:44,790
Hey, after all this,
are we even blood brothers?

83
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,430
Fine, forget it.

84
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:51,100
Never mind. Forget it.

85
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:54,600
No, it's not like that, brother.

86
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:56,300
"Brother?"

87
00:04:58,370 --> 00:05:01,170
Here, have a dried persimmon.

88
00:05:18,890 --> 00:05:20,930
How am I supposed
to cover this up again?

89
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,230
My goodness, Su Ah.

90
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:33,440
Wait, did you really set
all this up yourself, my sweetie?

91
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:41,110
Goodness. What is your dad doing?

92
00:05:41,350 --> 00:05:43,650
He is talking with Uncle Dae Chi
on the second floor.

93
00:05:44,650 --> 00:05:46,980
You should've called me
if you were hungry.

94
00:05:48,390 --> 00:05:50,020
The restaurant was packed
with dinner guests,

95
00:05:50,090 --> 00:05:51,490
so Grandma was a little late.

96
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:53,190
I'm sorry, sweetheart.

97
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,630
It is okay.

98
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:58,500
I know how to make a meal
for myself, Grandma.

99
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:00,770
You're so amazing,

100
00:06:01,130 --> 00:06:04,370
but Su Ah, who taught you
how to do all this?

101
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:07,310
A long time ago,
when Mom was working part-time...

102
00:06:07,310 --> 00:06:09,040
packaging things
at the shopping mall,

103
00:06:09,110 --> 00:06:10,240
she had to work late nights.

104
00:06:10,910 --> 00:06:13,280
Mom taught me everything back then.

105
00:06:13,810 --> 00:06:16,080
I want to fry an egg too,

106
00:06:16,150 --> 00:06:18,980
but Mom said it was dangerous,
so she would teach me later.

107
00:06:21,050 --> 00:06:23,050
Did my Su Ah want lettuce wraps
so much...

108
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,590
that you washed all the lettuce
by yourself?

109
00:06:26,690 --> 00:06:28,430
You should eat with me, Grandma.

110
00:06:28,490 --> 00:06:30,030
Mom said eating lettuce wraps
in the evening...

111
00:06:30,030 --> 00:06:31,930
helped you sleep well.

112
00:06:46,110 --> 00:06:47,180
That cruel girl.

113
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,650
She taught her to be so capable,

114
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,550
so where is she now,
and how is she even getting by?

115
00:06:55,190 --> 00:06:58,220
What? Gosh, I'm hungry.
Give me some food too.

116
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,390
What's this? There's no stew?

117
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,800
Do you not have hands?

118
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:08,530
If you are hungry, you can
make your own food or starve.

119
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:10,400
Did you do something great today?

120
00:07:11,070 --> 00:07:12,070
You ruined your own life,

121
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:14,140
so how dare you come here
demanding stew?

122
00:07:14,210 --> 00:07:15,740
You worthless brat.

123
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:23,050
Gosh, you used to make me
a full feast.

124
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:26,980
Su Ah,
what is wrong with your grandma?

125
00:07:34,430 --> 00:07:36,760
The whole house smells
like fermented soybean paste.

126
00:07:37,130 --> 00:07:39,360
- Did my mother-in-law order this?
- Yes.

127
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:42,030
She said Seung Yun liked it,
so that's what I prepared.

128
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:43,300
Here.

129
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:45,940
Quickly boil this in a pot.

130
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,670
I went all the way to Cheongdam-dong
to custom order this.

131
00:07:49,470 --> 00:07:50,640
Oh, okay.

132
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:55,850
We should make some salad, right?

133
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:57,780
Oh, and by the way.

134
00:07:57,780 --> 00:08:00,750
I marinated and cooked
the short ribs myself, got it?

135
00:08:01,290 --> 00:08:03,290
Why would I lie, ma'am?

136
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:06,660
Ma'am,

137
00:08:07,490 --> 00:08:09,890
doing as you are told is your job.

138
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:12,730
I told you when we first
signed the contract, right?

139
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,630
That I would pay you handsomely?

140
00:08:16,170 --> 00:08:17,240
Understood.

141
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:20,610
If Madam asks, I will tell her that.

142
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:39,060
Dad, you are home early.

143
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:40,890
Did Mom get off work too?

144
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:44,360
She came home as soon as
she heard Seung Yun made it home.

145
00:08:45,130 --> 00:08:47,670
Your mom is busy
in the kitchen right now.

146
00:08:48,730 --> 00:08:49,900
What about Grandma?

147
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:52,940
I think she is looking at
company documents on her laptop.

148
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:55,070
Mom's company or yours?

149
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:57,040
My company.

150
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,710
I'm so nervous.

151
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:02,750
I doubt she will say much.
I will wash up and come down.

152
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:04,320
Is Seung Yun on the second floor?

153
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:07,390
In Grandma's room.
You can see him at dinner.

154
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:08,950
I guess I should.

155
00:09:12,390 --> 00:09:13,390
Do Yun.

156
00:09:14,430 --> 00:09:15,960
I caught you red-handed today.

157
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:17,730
What?

158
00:09:18,030 --> 00:09:19,930
You like Manager Kang, don't you?

159
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:21,330
Me?

160
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:24,870
Hey, and since when
are you two so close?

161
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:27,200
Well, she feels like
an older sister.

162
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:31,940
And my intuition is right.
You are totally into her.

163
00:09:33,010 --> 00:09:34,250
Give me proof.

164
00:09:34,310 --> 00:09:36,550
She just brushed off what happened
back then as a simple incident...

165
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:37,780
and isn't even thinking about it.

166
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:39,580
But you are the only one...

167
00:09:39,650 --> 00:09:42,690
thinking about it every day,
thinking about her,

168
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:44,760
and you even dragged me along...

169
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:46,420
to explain that
you weren't a pervert.

170
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:52,060
You are a very busy person
who lived only for work.

171
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:54,600
"Lived?"

172
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:56,170
Why is that in the past tense?

173
00:09:57,340 --> 00:09:59,470
You're already interested in her.

174
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:02,170
You should be trying to impress her,

175
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,180
but you hated being labeled
a pervert more than death,

176
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,410
which is why you did that today.

177
00:10:06,010 --> 00:10:08,080
It was just unfair
and uncomfortable,

178
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:10,750
and I normally can't stand
things like that.

179
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,120
- End of story.
- Before you go to sleep,

180
00:10:13,850 --> 00:10:17,720
think about her and put a hand
on your chest.

181
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:20,190
I bet your heart rate will speed up.

182
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:23,160
Anyway, I'll put your card
to good use.

183
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,500
Hey, exactly how much
are you planning to spend?

184
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:38,010
Team Leader Cha.

185
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:40,980
I brought some work home
to look over,

186
00:10:41,050 --> 00:10:42,810
and I have a few questions.

187
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:45,220
Are you available for a quick call?

188
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:50,420
(Are you available
for a quick call?)

189
00:10:52,660 --> 00:10:54,230
Unless it is an emergency,

190
00:10:54,230 --> 00:10:56,030
for any work-related questions
after working hours,

191
00:10:56,090 --> 00:10:58,300
please use the AI chatbot,
Assistant Manager Kang.

192
00:10:58,630 --> 00:11:01,800
What?
He's completely shutting me out.

193
00:11:02,230 --> 00:11:03,570
So this is how you want to play it?

194
00:11:04,270 --> 00:11:05,570
Now I'm feeling competitive.

195
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,970
Sweetie, who is shutting you out?

196
00:11:08,970 --> 00:11:10,310
And why are you feeling competitive?

197
00:11:10,310 --> 00:11:11,480
It's nothing.

198
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:14,810
- Ye Ri. Hey.
- Leave her alone.

199
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:17,620
Stop trying to pry
into every little thing she does.

200
00:11:18,650 --> 00:11:20,180
I'm just curious.

201
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,390
Before we move,

202
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:26,020
throw this sofa away.

203
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:29,460
I'll get a disposal sticker
from the community center.

204
00:11:30,530 --> 00:11:31,630
Why would we throw the sofa away?

205
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:36,770
Are you planning to bring this
to a tiny apartment?

206
00:11:37,170 --> 00:11:38,370
Will you sleep with it on your head?

207
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,110
Then without a sofa,

208
00:11:41,110 --> 00:11:42,440
do you expect me
to sit on the floor?

209
00:11:42,510 --> 00:11:44,410
Me? The Park Ji Young?

210
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,950
No way. We are taking it.

211
00:11:50,010 --> 00:11:52,050
- I will sleep with it on my head.
- Do whatever you want.

212
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:53,880
Sleep with it on your head
or boil it and eat it.

213
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:02,690
I'm home.

214
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:06,660
What's that, Aunt Ri Ja?

215
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:09,330
It's a stepper.
Don't you know what this is?

216
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:11,500
Did you buy a new one?

217
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:16,440
Hey, are you making fun of me?

218
00:12:16,510 --> 00:12:18,680
I have never even seen
my own paycheck,

219
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:20,580
and I'm living off your grandma.

220
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:25,580
I bought it secondhand online,
okay? Happy?

221
00:12:25,650 --> 00:12:27,350
It's brand new and unopened.

222
00:12:30,050 --> 00:12:32,590
What's with that annoying smile?

223
00:12:34,290 --> 00:12:35,530
Nothing.

224
00:12:35,590 --> 00:12:38,830
It's just that you seem to rely
on fancy gear to exercise.

225
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:42,000
You are always jumping
from one thing to another.

226
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:44,440
Wait until you get to my age, kid.

227
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:46,840
In life, having the right gear
is everything.

228
00:12:48,710 --> 00:12:49,810
Hey.

229
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:51,810
Did you buy a scarf?

230
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:54,780
Oh my, what has gotten
into our little cheapskate?

231
00:12:54,850 --> 00:12:56,910
I was just throwing
the idea out there.

232
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:01,020
My sister will finally have
a reason to smile today.

233
00:13:01,550 --> 00:13:04,220
She can finally enjoy the perks
of having a good daughter.

234
00:13:04,290 --> 00:13:07,590
Of course.
Hey, you go inside first, okay?

235
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:10,160
Hurry up and show your mom.
I'll finish up here and head in.

236
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:11,800
Okay.

237
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:15,370
- But Aunt Ri Ja...
- Yes?

238
00:13:15,430 --> 00:13:17,400
Your clothes look a bit too tight.

239
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,540
I'm not sure
if you can even breathe in them.

240
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,080
Oh, seriously.

241
00:13:25,410 --> 00:13:28,480
She always has to say
something to get on my nerves.

242
00:13:29,050 --> 00:13:30,050
Seriously.

243
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:35,990
How can all my children
be like this?

244
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,060
You immature girl.

245
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:41,060
When have I ever worn things
like this and dressed up?

246
00:13:42,590 --> 00:13:45,060
And how much was this anyway?

247
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:47,300
(Health Checkup Voucher:
3,000 dollars)

248
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:48,570
Three thousand?

249
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,770
You must have money to burn.

250
00:13:51,770 --> 00:13:53,800
Mom, let me say something too.

251
00:13:54,310 --> 00:13:57,470
You have been suffering
because of Gang Nam and Dae Chi,

252
00:13:57,740 --> 00:14:00,340
so I wanted to give you
something nice.

253
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:03,250
I made up my mind
and prepared this for you,

254
00:14:03,310 --> 00:14:05,450
so why are you jumping
down my throat?

255
00:14:06,050 --> 00:14:08,350
Why are you taking
all your anger out on me?

256
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:14,530
Did I get divorced and move back in?

257
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:17,160
Did I cause a financial accident?

258
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:21,030
And Mom,
this health checkup voucher is...

259
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:22,330
I've heard enough.

260
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,800
Take it all back
and get a refund, you brat.

261
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,200
You're right.

262
00:14:27,470 --> 00:14:29,370
Your mom is burning up
inside right now.

263
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:31,410
My insides are so burnt...

264
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:34,710
that it's a miracle my bones
and joints haven't turned to ash.

265
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:36,780
This is so ridiculous.

266
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:40,080
You paid 800 dollars
for this piece of cloth?

267
00:14:41,150 --> 00:14:43,920
That's absolutely ridiculous.

268
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:47,630
It's a designer brand,
and it's top quality, too.

269
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:50,630
I bought it with a 30 percent
employee discount.

270
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:53,260
That still means you paid
over 500 dollars for it, right?

271
00:14:56,630 --> 00:14:58,000
If I were you,

272
00:14:58,770 --> 00:15:02,110
and if you cared even a tenth
or a hundredth about how I felt,

273
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:04,910
you would've saved every penny...

274
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:06,880
and shown me
you were living responsibly.

275
00:15:07,510 --> 00:15:10,110
Instead, you're wasting money
on things like this.

276
00:15:11,150 --> 00:15:14,290
Gang Nam and Dae Chi
are both struggling right now,

277
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:16,420
so do you think
I want to enjoy this luxury?

278
00:15:16,890 --> 00:15:18,390
I only have one daughter,

279
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,720
and she doesn't understand
her mother at all.

280
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:28,330
Mom, when have I ever
been extravagant?

281
00:15:28,870 --> 00:15:33,300
I thought long and hard about this
to comfort you, Mom.

282
00:15:36,170 --> 00:15:37,810
Do my feelings mean nothing to you?

283
00:15:43,450 --> 00:15:46,420
Do you want me to show
you my savings account right now?

284
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:53,020
Why didn't I think of that?

285
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,160
I'm so stupid.

286
00:15:57,330 --> 00:15:58,330
Fine.

287
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:01,470
I was wrong.

288
00:16:02,470 --> 00:16:03,670
I will get a refund.

289
00:16:04,170 --> 00:16:05,440
I will get a refund...

290
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,770
and give it to you in cash.
Happy now?

291
00:16:10,810 --> 00:16:12,910
And Mom,
this health checkup voucher...

292
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:15,380
was a gift
from a long-time VIP customer...

293
00:16:15,450 --> 00:16:17,010
before they went on a trip.

294
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,380
I didn't spend a single dollar
of my own money on it,

295
00:16:20,820 --> 00:16:22,220
so keep it and make sure you use it.

296
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:33,630
But Mom, do you know what?

297
00:16:33,930 --> 00:16:36,470
You're taking all your anger
at Gang Nam and Dae Chi...

298
00:16:37,030 --> 00:16:39,000
out on me right now.

299
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:42,140
I was only trying to do
something nice for you.

300
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:45,240
You don't say a single word to them,

301
00:16:45,310 --> 00:16:48,680
but you take it out on me
when I'm working myself to death.

302
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:53,050
You're a woman too.

303
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:55,650
Do you think your daughter
is that easy of a target?

304
00:17:14,410 --> 00:17:15,410
Hold on.

305
00:17:16,470 --> 00:17:18,410
I can understand Gang Nam,

306
00:17:20,010 --> 00:17:23,110
but did something happen
with Dae Chi too?

307
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:26,580
Then again,

308
00:17:27,150 --> 00:17:28,750
time is the best teacher.

309
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:31,320
Soon Deok,

310
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:34,590
you could set up shop
as a fortune teller now.

311
00:17:35,130 --> 00:17:36,230
Goodness.

312
00:17:36,490 --> 00:17:40,160
Mrs. Choi, do you need anything?
Did my sister forget your water?

313
00:17:41,430 --> 00:17:42,430
What is it?

314
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:45,270
Don't say a word.

315
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:54,110
Grandma.

316
00:17:54,510 --> 00:17:57,380
It's late.
Hurry upstairs and go to sleep.

317
00:18:03,550 --> 00:18:04,920
What is wrong with her?

318
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:09,690
Hey, why did you bring that out?

319
00:18:10,330 --> 00:18:11,530
This is because of you.

320
00:18:12,330 --> 00:18:13,430
I don't want to talk about it.

321
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:14,970
Goodness.

322
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:19,500
What's with that girl? Unbelievable.

323
00:18:36,190 --> 00:18:37,320
Mi Mi,

324
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:41,560
that scarf Da Mi bought,

325
00:18:41,630 --> 00:18:43,330
why did you not accept it?

326
00:18:44,130 --> 00:18:46,230
She probably made a big decision...

327
00:18:46,300 --> 00:18:48,770
and used her employee discount
to buy it.

328
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:52,670
Don't tell me you put her up to it,
Jo Ri Ja.

329
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:54,670
You did, didn't you?

330
00:18:55,810 --> 00:18:57,140
I knew it.

331
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:58,340
Unless it is life and death,

332
00:18:58,410 --> 00:19:00,110
that cheapskate
won't even take a taxi.

333
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:02,380
I was wondering why she suddenly
did something so crazy.

334
00:19:03,150 --> 00:19:05,880
Why are you always
blaming innocent people?

335
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:11,260
I mean, Da Mi was just...

336
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:15,930
worrying about what to get her mom,
so I asked how a scarf would be.

337
00:19:15,990 --> 00:19:17,730
That was it.

338
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:21,870
I just gave her one piece of advice
as her aunt.

339
00:19:21,930 --> 00:19:23,300
I mean it.

340
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:24,570
Do you think I don't know you?

341
00:19:25,370 --> 00:19:27,500
Don't try to weasel
your way out of this.

342
00:19:28,970 --> 00:19:30,240
Fine.

343
00:19:30,310 --> 00:19:33,110
That cheapskate was being
a little annoying,

344
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:34,850
and you were feeling down
because of Gang Nam,

345
00:19:34,910 --> 00:19:37,280
so I told her to comfort you
and spend some money. So what?

346
00:19:37,350 --> 00:19:39,180
Is that really something
to be yelled at for?

347
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,420
Seriously.

348
00:19:57,730 --> 00:19:58,840
But hey,

349
00:19:59,470 --> 00:20:01,670
I think Mrs. Choi...

350
00:20:02,610 --> 00:20:05,340
was listening at the door earlier.

351
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:08,410
What?

352
00:20:09,010 --> 00:20:11,620
Since when? How much did she hear?

353
00:20:11,950 --> 00:20:15,890
Well, I don't know.
I came in the middle of it.

354
00:20:17,590 --> 00:20:18,790
We are in trouble.

355
00:20:19,190 --> 00:20:20,620
What should we do?

356
00:20:24,630 --> 00:20:26,760
Drink slowly, sweetie.

357
00:20:27,130 --> 00:20:30,530
There is no cure
for choking on water.

358
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:32,400
Oh my.

359
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:35,740
Lie down.

360
00:20:39,410 --> 00:20:41,010
- Great-Grandma.
- Yes.

361
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:43,980
Please scratch my back,
so I can sleep.

362
00:20:44,050 --> 00:20:45,820
Okay, I got it, sweetie.

363
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:49,120
You have to keep scratching...

364
00:20:49,190 --> 00:20:52,760
- until I fall asleep.
- Okay, my little puppy.

365
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:56,730
But what did you eat for dinner
to be drinking so much water?

366
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:58,300
Lettuce wraps.

367
00:20:58,760 --> 00:21:01,530
I think I ate
too much soybean paste.

368
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:04,640
Mom told me not to eat salty food.

369
00:21:07,270 --> 00:21:09,410
You miss your mom a lot, right?

370
00:21:12,010 --> 00:21:13,880
I'm sleepy, Great-Grandma.

371
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:16,180
Good night.

372
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:18,620
Oh my.

373
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:21,420
The adults are the sinners...

374
00:21:23,350 --> 00:21:25,290
for making this
innocent child suffer.

375
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:31,360
But what is going on with Dae Chi?

376
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,030
Then again,

377
00:21:36,330 --> 00:21:40,170
a tree with many branches
never has a windless day.

378
00:22:00,690 --> 00:22:02,560
Goodness, Da Mi.

379
00:22:03,930 --> 00:22:05,330
You can't even rest after work.

380
00:22:06,130 --> 00:22:07,630
Are you preparing
for a contest again?

381
00:22:09,130 --> 00:22:10,530
Or an internship?

382
00:22:11,770 --> 00:22:14,440
Gosh, you are really persistent.

383
00:22:15,110 --> 00:22:16,440
What company is it this time?

384
00:22:18,340 --> 00:22:21,340
Since when did you
have so much interest in me?

385
00:22:21,980 --> 00:22:23,350
What do you want to say?

386
00:22:23,410 --> 00:22:27,080
I'm just so disappointed.
I can't even sleep.

387
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:31,990
It's about Dae Chi.

388
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:36,730
He's the one among us
who has the most money.

389
00:22:37,430 --> 00:22:40,230
So earlier, putting my pride aside,

390
00:22:40,300 --> 00:22:42,800
I asked him to help me out
with some money...

391
00:22:43,270 --> 00:22:45,340
for the first time in my life.

392
00:22:46,940 --> 00:22:48,740
He cut me off right away.

393
00:22:50,040 --> 00:22:51,940
He said that between siblings...

394
00:22:51,940 --> 00:22:54,410
No, between family members,

395
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:56,850
he refuses to lend or borrow money.

396
00:22:56,910 --> 00:22:58,520
He says it's his belief.

397
00:22:59,150 --> 00:23:01,280
How could he do this to me?

398
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:04,590
Da Mi, don't you think
he's going a little overboard?

399
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:07,920
Gang Nam, Dae Chi is also...

400
00:23:10,090 --> 00:23:11,700
No, never mind.

401
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:15,930
So what I was trying to say is,

402
00:23:16,630 --> 00:23:19,340
since that jerk Dae Chi won't help,

403
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:22,940
if you have any extra money,
could you help me...

404
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:24,710
Are you starting another business?

405
00:23:24,980 --> 00:23:27,740
After ruining so many,
have you still not come to your senses?

406
00:23:28,150 --> 00:23:31,180
You should just
think about getting a job somewhere.

407
00:23:35,550 --> 00:23:37,890
Forget it.
Keep doing what you were doing.

408
00:23:38,160 --> 00:23:39,160
Go on.

409
00:23:42,630 --> 00:23:43,890
Gang Nam, stop.

410
00:23:44,390 --> 00:23:46,200
Why?

411
00:23:46,430 --> 00:23:47,830
Take off your pants.

412
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:50,100
Suddenly? My pants?

413
00:23:50,300 --> 00:23:52,500
Gosh, you're about
to expose yourself.

414
00:23:52,570 --> 00:23:53,740
Expose myself? What?

415
00:23:56,570 --> 00:23:58,180
You really are something else.

416
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:01,510
But this is...

417
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:05,520
the only pair of pajamas I have.

418
00:24:09,650 --> 00:24:11,420
Then, Madam, I will...

419
00:24:11,490 --> 00:24:13,390
Good work, Mrs. Anseong.

420
00:24:16,390 --> 00:24:18,930
Goodness, even braised short ribs?

421
00:24:19,530 --> 00:24:20,800
Did you make this?

422
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:22,570
Seung Yun has returned
to the country,

423
00:24:22,630 --> 00:24:25,040
and it is the first time the whole family
is gathering for a meal.

424
00:24:25,100 --> 00:24:26,870
I couldn't just let it pass.

425
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:29,410
I decided to show off my skills
for the first time in a while.

426
00:24:30,910 --> 00:24:32,710
Eat up, Seung Yun.

427
00:24:33,010 --> 00:24:34,040
I will.

428
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:35,750
You never make things
like this for us.

429
00:24:36,250 --> 00:24:38,050
Mom, you're playing
favorites too much.

430
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:40,120
It smells good.

431
00:24:41,350 --> 00:24:43,250
You must be busy enough
with work at the company.

432
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:44,620
Thank you for the meal,
Aunt Jin Hee.

433
00:24:47,190 --> 00:24:49,030
Seung Yun, after we eat,

434
00:24:49,030 --> 00:24:50,630
let's have a drink together
on the second floor.

435
00:24:50,690 --> 00:24:53,300
I've been saving something special
to celebrate your return.

436
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:55,170
Sure, let's do that.

437
00:24:56,170 --> 00:24:57,700
Mother...

438
00:24:58,600 --> 00:25:02,340
Why are you not saying anything?
Are you uncomfortable?

439
00:25:02,740 --> 00:25:04,070
I'm fine.

440
00:25:04,070 --> 00:25:06,340
The whole family is gathered,
and that is all that matters.

441
00:25:06,540 --> 00:25:08,550
What more does an old woman
have to say?

442
00:25:09,250 --> 00:25:10,450
Eat up, everyone.

443
00:25:11,050 --> 00:25:12,320
- Yes.
- Yes.

444
00:25:19,160 --> 00:25:21,890
The fermented soybean paste stew
is incredibly savory.

445
00:25:21,890 --> 00:25:24,590
- What?
- That lady must be a good cook.

446
00:25:25,160 --> 00:25:27,860
We have someone flawless.

447
00:25:28,530 --> 00:25:31,940
Even her seasoned vegetables
are seasoned perfectly.

448
00:25:32,870 --> 00:25:36,610
Oh, try wrapping your food
in those pumpkin leaves, Seung Yun.

449
00:25:36,670 --> 00:25:37,940
- Yes, Grandma.
- Good boy.

450
00:25:40,940 --> 00:25:43,250
You have to acknowledge
my mom's skills too, Grandma.

451
00:25:43,480 --> 00:25:44,680
It's melting in my mouth.

452
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:46,720
Seung Yun, try this too.

453
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:49,390
I'll take my time.

454
00:25:49,450 --> 00:25:52,020
Mother, you should try some too.

455
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,420
I will eat on my own.

456
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:56,960
Let's see.

457
00:26:00,760 --> 00:26:01,800
What?

458
00:26:03,700 --> 00:26:06,140
What's wrong, Mother?

459
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:10,310
Which butcher did you get this from?

460
00:26:11,810 --> 00:26:15,510
From the department store food hall
we always go to...

461
00:26:15,510 --> 00:26:17,050
Don't ever go there again.

462
00:26:17,510 --> 00:26:19,750
Look at all this grease
floating around.

463
00:26:20,650 --> 00:26:21,720
It's ruined.

464
00:26:23,550 --> 00:26:24,550
Yes, Mother.

465
00:26:26,760 --> 00:26:28,960
Seung Yun,
when do you start working...

466
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:29,990
at the apparel company?

467
00:26:30,460 --> 00:26:32,930
I plan to rest for two or three days
before I start, Uncle In Sung.

468
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:34,630
That soon?

469
00:26:35,270 --> 00:26:37,430
All you did was work in the States.

470
00:26:37,500 --> 00:26:39,100
You can take plenty of time to rest.

471
00:26:39,370 --> 00:26:41,000
I was going to have you take...

472
00:26:41,070 --> 00:26:44,140
some herbal medicine
before you started working.

473
00:26:44,410 --> 00:26:46,280
She's right. What's the rush?

474
00:26:46,340 --> 00:26:48,980
Get some rest.
Spend some time with Grandma, too.

475
00:26:49,980 --> 00:26:51,610
Am I a child?

476
00:26:52,420 --> 00:26:54,720
You don't need to entertain me.

477
00:26:55,420 --> 00:26:56,850
Take a few days
to catch your breath,

478
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:59,960
and get right to work, Seung Yun.

479
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:02,560
Don't worry about me.

480
00:27:04,230 --> 00:27:05,230
Yes, Grandma.

481
00:27:08,030 --> 00:27:11,070
Mom, I think Grandma
is a little mad.

482
00:27:12,540 --> 00:27:13,570
Eat your food.

483
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:20,810
What's the point of living
in a palace like this?

484
00:27:21,980 --> 00:27:24,250
What good is having
a mountain of wealth?

485
00:27:24,850 --> 00:27:28,620
When you pass away,
you can't take it with you.

486
00:27:31,990 --> 00:27:33,890
The burden on Madam's heart...

487
00:27:34,490 --> 00:27:36,090
must be so heavy.

488
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:40,460
They're so beautiful.

489
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:44,430
No wonder this family's
eldest grandson is so handsome.

490
00:27:44,430 --> 00:27:45,570
Mrs. Anseong.

491
00:27:49,770 --> 00:27:50,870
Madam.

492
00:27:54,510 --> 00:27:56,610
I'm so sorry...

493
00:27:56,610 --> 00:27:59,680
Do you even know what sorry means?

494
00:28:13,630 --> 00:28:16,530
(Mission: Mompossible)

495
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:19,470
My only children are Do Yun
and my daughter, Se Na.

496
00:28:19,540 --> 00:28:21,040
Just the two of them.

497
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:22,810
It will always be
just the two of them.

498
00:28:22,870 --> 00:28:25,710
My gosh, how could you not
recognize your role model...

499
00:28:25,780 --> 00:28:28,110
when he was right in front of you?
And more than once, too?

500
00:28:28,550 --> 00:28:29,550
Kang Da Mi...

501
00:28:29,550 --> 00:28:32,150
I should've just given him my number
when he asked for it.

502
00:28:33,620 --> 00:28:35,620
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
